          "id": "1765177952817",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765177952818_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "DISPLAY_DATA:\n{{$context.$nodes.PREPARE_BUYING_GROUP_DISPLAY_DATA.$output.result}}\n\nTASK:\nCreate a multiRecordWidget for the Buying Group Definition section using DISPLAY_DATA.rows exactly.\n\nRows and columns:\n- DISPLAY_DATA.rows is already display-ready. Each row already contains the exact final cell values.\n- Use DISPLAY_DATA.columns exactly as the table column order.\n- For every table row, copy these exact fields verbatim from DISPLAY_DATA.rows: \"Buyer Role\", \"Persona\", \"# of Accounts With Role\", \"Percentage\".\n- Do not read alternate raw fields. Do not infer or recalculate metrics. Do not drop the denominator from \"# of Accounts With Role\".\n- \"# of Accounts With Role\" must include the full fraction string exactly as provided, for example \"12835/8576\", not just \"12835\".\n- \"Percentage\" must copy the provided value exactly, including values over 100%.\n- Never rename, translate, normalize, replace, or invent Buyer Role or Persona values.\n- If DISPLAY_DATA.rows is empty, return the required columns with no invented data rows.\n\nOutput Requirements:\n- Use a multiRecordWidget with columns in this exact order: \"Buyer Role\", \"Persona\", \"# of Accounts With Role\", \"Percentage\".\n- Keep the title and executive description behavior consistent with the prior Buying Group Definition widget: generate a concise outcome-oriented title and a 2-3 sentence executive summary from DISPLAY_DATA.rows.\n- Do not generate prose outside the widget.\n- Return only the completed widget.\n\nGeneral Requirements:\n- Maintain consistent formatting.\n- Do not include commentary, explanations, markdown, or additional sections."
            },
            {
              "id": "1765177952817_systemPrompt",
              "name": "systemPrompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Generate the multiRecordWidget format. Output must be only oraInfoDisplay and no other text"
            }
          ],
